import crate::expr_text::expr_text
import crate::pattern_text::pattern_text
import redox_ast::{Binding, Expr}

-- | A binding — `n = 0`, `mut n = 0`, `n : u64 = 0`.
-- |
-- | # The separator is one colon, everywhere — and §3 row 8 is now moot
-- |
-- | Row 8 read *"a binding's `::` type annotation → spaced — `n : u64 = 0`"*,
-- | and `n : u64 = 0` never parsed: `try_binding` has always read a single
-- | `TokenKind::Colon`. The local binding was the one form spelled with `:`
-- | while a signature, a `const` item and an ascription took a spaced `::`.
-- |
-- | Plan 52 collapsed that: `:` annotates a type in every position and `::`
-- | joins a path and nothing else, so the three forms below differ only in
-- | what surrounds them.
-- |
-- | | Form | Separator | |
-- | |---|---|---|
-- | | A local binding | `:` | `n : u64 = 0` — this function |
-- | | A `const` or `static` item | `:` | `threshold : f64 = 0.5` — leaf 2's |
-- | | An expression ascription | `:` | `(1 + 2) : u64` — leaf 3's |
-- |
-- | So row 8's *rule* — never tighten a spaced `::`, because tightening it
-- | changed an ascription into a path — no longer has anything to protect: the
-- | two are different tokens now. §10 records the correction.
-- |
-- | # A block-valued binding has nothing after its `=`
-- |
-- | Plan 55 leaf 7 retired `do`, and `do` was what used to fill that space:
-- | `inner = do` then an indented block. With the keyword gone the block
-- | begins on the *next* line, so `= ` would leave a trailing space on this
-- | one — which `treefmt` strips and the round-trip then fails on. The
-- | separator is therefore chosen by the value's form, which is the only place
-- | in this printer where it is.
-- |
-- | A **labelled** block still has something to write — `found = 'search` —
-- | so it takes the ordinary separator.
export(crate) binding_text : &Binding -> usize -> &str -> String
binding_text binding indent source =
  prefix = if binding.is_mut
    "mut "
  else
    ""
  ty = case &binding.ty of
    Some ty -> format! \-> " : #{ty.text}"
    None -> String::new ()
  separator = case &binding.value of
    Expr::Block { label = None, .. } -> "=\n"
    _ -> "= "
  pattern = pattern_text (&binding.pattern)
  value = expr_text (&binding.value) 0 indent source
  format! \-> "#{prefix}#{pattern}#{ty} #{separator}#{value}"
